  "lore": {
    "A": {
      "title": "The Herbalist's Diary",
      "text": "Day 9. The caps are warm to the touch. Day 14. The caps turn to follow my lamp. Day 20. I have stopped eating them. I think they have started eating me."
    },
    "Y": {
      "title": "Scrawled Near the Pens",
      "text": "THE SHAMBLERS WERE MINERS. DON'T LET THEM BREATHE ON YOU. DON'T LET THEM GET CLOSE ENOUGH TO TRY."
    },
    "R": {
      "title": "The Mother's Root",
      "text": "Under the throne the Mother keeps her oldest root, and the root keeps a secret: rot is only life deciding to start over. Learn to refuse it, and you will not start over before you are finished.",
      "teaches": "fungal_art"
    },
    "G": {
      "title": "The Voice of the Ancients",
      "text": "Here, the walls speak of forgotten secrets. Listen closely, and the wainscoting reveals tales of those who dared to delve deeper, their fates intertwined with the fungal whispers. Each groan of the wood is a warning, each creak a message from beyond the veil of the deeps."
    },
    "M": {
      "title": "A Haven for the Spores",
      "text": "Here, the spores dance in the air, carried by the breath of the ancient toadstool. Those who seek the essence of the deep must leave their worries at the entrance, for this bower is a sanctuary where life thrives in death."
    },
    "O": {
      "title": "The Foul Cloister",
      "text": "Here the spores thicken the air, choking out light and life. Inscriptions warn of the creeping corruption that lurks in the shadows, whispering of forgotten rites and dark sorceries."
    },
    "U": {
      "title": "The Weaving Silence",
      "text": "Silken strands crisscross the room, catching the light in intricate patterns. A faint, rhythmic clicking echoes from the darkest corner, the work of unseen weavers."
    },
    "X": {
      "title": "The Vault of Fungal Secrets",
      "text": "Here, the air is thick with the promise of growth. A rare spore, said to grant immortality, is said to be hidden within these walls. Few return from this chamber, and fewer still are willing to speak of what they find."
    }
  },
  "riddles": {
    "?": {
      "title": "The Riddle of Rotting Vein",
      "question": "I have a cap but no head, a ring but no finger, and I grow in the dark. What am I?",
